   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## WEB2 Klein: style match and edit (images in)\nEdit a pick with words, or make a new image that matches a direction's look from reference images.\n\n- **Image 1** is `<ref_image_0>`: the image to edit. The output keeps its aspect (1.5 MP).\n- Images 2-3 are muted. Select one, **Ctrl+M** to unmute. Refer to them as `<ref_image_1>`, `<ref_image_2>`. More refs: drag new Load Image nodes into the empty `images` slots (up to 10).\n- **Edit:** *Keep the composition, subject and camera of <ref_image_0>. Change ... Keep everything else.*\n- **Style match:** *A [new subject] in exactly the palette, lighting, grain and rendering style of <ref_image_0> and <ref_image_1>.* Use the direction's hero as ref 0 so a set stays consistent.\n- **Make room for copy:** *Extend the empty background on the left third of <ref_image_0> so it is clean and uncluttered.*\n- Distilled model, 16 steps, CFG 1 (~35 s). Compare slider shows before / after."
   ]
  },
